      "statement": "Produce a measurable exact proximal selector p satisfying p+eta*gradientV(p)=y, the quantitative quadratic minimum and uniqueness, and equal-eta nonexpansivity. The literal G(s,z)=gradientV(p_s+sqrt(eta_s)*z) is jointly measurable and has equal-eta input/noise Lipschitz constants 1 and sqrteta. Produce the genuine Markov law K_s=G(s,-)_#stdGaussian with vector first Bochner moment. For its own mean m_s, every a and signed t have an integrable exponential and integral <=exp(eta_s*t^2*norm(a)^2/2). This covers (3.2) and (4.3)-(4.5), without identifying K with the RGO posterior or HMC transition.",
      "formula": "F_s(x)=V(x)+\\|x-y_s\\|^2/(2\\eta_s),\\quad p_s+\\eta_s\\nabla V(p_s)=y_s,\\quad G(s,z)=\\nabla V(p_s+\\sqrt{\\eta_s}z),\\quad K_s=G(s,\\cdot)_\\#\\gamma,\\quad m_s=\\int w\\,dK_s,\\quad\\int e^{t\\langle a,w-m_s\\rangle}dK_s\\le e^{\\eta_st^2\\|a\\|^2/2}.",
      "steps": [
