    "candidate_assumptions": [
      {
        "source": "Euclidean d-dimensional source beta1/alpha=kappa^-1 and eta>0; exact argmin and Gaussian gradient definition.",
        "lean": "Source beta=1, alpha=kappa^-1, real kappa>=1; actual C2 V with kappa^-1*normv^2 <= D2V(x)[v,v] <= normv^2 for every x,v.\nFinite real complete Hilbert/Borel full space E, including dimension zero; arbitrary measurable parameter space S; actual measurable eta:S->R and y:S->E with eta(s)>0 for every s. These coordinate-free/parameter-space extensions are disclosed. Printed Lemma4.2 inherits eta>0 from Section3.1; the eta<=1 premise of neighboring Lemma4.1 is not consumed.\nNo supplied proximal point, minimizer, measurable selector, gradient estimate, Lipschitz bound, probability kernel, mean or concentration certificate. Exact witnesses, first moments, signed Laplace domains and sharp coefficient are produced internally. The numerical proximal call cap eta<=1/(2 beta) remains a separate computational contract."
      },
      {
        "source": "Actual proximal existence/uniqueness/optimality are implicit and source uses fixed-eta nonexpansivity.",
        "lean": "The constructed pointwise damped fixed point supplies measurable selector, true equation and unique quadratic minimum internally."
      },
      {
        "source": "Actual estimator (3.2), sharp centered concentration (4.3), input/noise Lipschitz (4.4)-(4.5).",
        "lean": "Produce a measurable exact proximal selector p satisfying p+eta*gradientV(p)=y, the quantitative quadratic minimum and uniqueness, and equal-eta nonexpansivity. The literal G(s,z)=gradientV(p_s+sqrt(eta_s)*z) is jointly measurable and has equal-eta input/noise Lipschitz constants 1 and sqrteta. Produce the genuine Markov law K_s=G(s,-)_#stdGaussian with vector first Bochner moment. For its own mean m_s, every a and signed t have an integrable exponential and integral <=exp(eta_s*t^2*norm(a)^2/2). This covers (3.2) and (4.3)-(4.5), without identifying K with the RGO posterior or HMC transition."
      },
      {
        "source": "Bias, first W2 bound, posterior/HMC semantics, higher algorithms and main/work/composition.",
        "lean": "Locally compiled sharp centered Gaussian-output estimate (4.3), retained exact positive-step proximal/evaluator and (4.4)-(4.5), genuine first Bochner moments and all signed exponential domains. Independent mathematics/blind/source/publication/exact-commit/integration admission pending. Bias (4.2), first W2 inequality in (4.6), LSI/T2 adapter, full Lemma4.2, higher smoothing/Picard/Wp/proxy-warmness/initialization, PBPS invariance/nonexplosion/hypocoercivity/implementation/work, both main results and actual-input precision/expected-query-cost composition remain open. Centers are actual Gaussian output means. TV proximity does not transfer unbounded expected cost."
      },
      {
        "source": "Section3.1 eta>0 and Lemma4.2 have no upper eta bound; neighboring Lemma4.1 alone requires eta<=1.",
        "lean": "Every eta>0 and all original C2/Hessian/parameter binders retained; signed domain and exact sharp bound are derived outputs."
      },
      {
        "source": "Actual centered Gaussian-gradient noise (4.3), xi=G-EgammaG, any direction u; no finite-mean/Laplace hypotheses printed.",
        "lean": "Actual own-mean Bochner/Laplace domains internally produced; coefficient eta*t^2*norm(a)^2/2 independently established by actual standard-Gaussian background."
      }
    ]
  },
